    "title": "Noble Elementary reunion brings 50-year-old memories to life - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Anja Wuolu ,\n18 hours ago\nFifty years after graduating from sixth grade, former students from Noble Elementary School in Golden Valley reunited with their teachers Sept. 28 to share memories, classroom stories and songs from their youth.\n\"Tears of joy did roll as students found and hugged their past teachers and shared life stories whether of childhood classroom memories or professional and family stories all happening while enjoying coffee and a wonderful variety of breakfast rolls,\" former teacher Audrey Kramer described. \"Abundant classroom memorabilia was displayed on long tables to bring back past moments at Noble, and also displayed were free standing oversized sixth grade 1975 classroom photos.\"\nKramer said since people have changed in appearance after 50 years, name tags were utilized to facilitate the event.\nA former student read tributes to each teacher. The former music teacher led the group in songs. The current principal led the group on a tour throughout the school.\nOver 100 former students and 31 former teachers were invited. Tracking everyone down, living or deceased was the achievement of former student Tom Matkovits. In total, 37 students and 10 teachers attended.",
